{"archetypes":[{"name":"waterfall-routing","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff rewires multi-vendor reviewer dispatch, fallback suppression, and dropped-slot propagation across several shell scripts.","prompt_body":"Investigate the end-to-end reviewer routing contract across dispatch-panel.sh, dispatch-with-waterfall outputs, review-core.sh, and the related tests. Focus on vendor availability combinations, conditional --no-fallback behavior, Codex phase-1 enablement, and whether dropped peer slots are forwarded without being mistaken for fatal infrastructure failures. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"threshold-math","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The change replaces fixed six-slot threshold logic with caller-supplied denominators, dropped slots, retry outputs, and per-archetype coverage checks.","prompt_body":"Trace the reviewer failure threshold calculations and normalization helpers for static, dynamic, dropped, phase2, phase3, and retry output names. Verify that 4-slot and 8-slot panels fail at the intended boundaries and that a whole archetype cannot silently disappear despite aggregate pass math. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"prompt-context","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"The folded plan-fidelity behavior depends on broader plan injection into reviewer-testing prompts, including untrusted plan and feature content.","prompt_body":"Review prompt rendering changes for reviewer-testing plan and feature injection across diff modes and description mode. Look for unintended context expansion to other specialists, malformed delimiter handling, or ways untrusted plan or diff content could alter reviewer instructions beyond the intended data boundary. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"artifact-policy","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The new static Codex outputs require precise log retention and exclusion behavior without dropping dynamic Codex evidence.","prompt_body":"Inspect round-log artifact inclusion and exclusion rules for static Codex specialist outputs, their sidecars, phased outputs, and dynamic Codex twins. Verify that the canonical aggregate artifacts remain sufficient for debugging while raw static transcripts are excluded consistently with Cursor behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sync-surfaces","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"The change touches generated prompts, topology projections, public docs, diagrams, and sync harnesses that can drift independently.","prompt_body":"Check generated and hand-maintained synchronization surfaces for stale panel-shape wording, regenerated pre-rendered reviewer bodies, manifest hashes, topology output, and documentation harness expectations. Pay special attention to places where generator-safe phrasing differs from the public canonical phrase. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
